<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45204" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stăbĭlīmentum</span></b> ,
		i, n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				stay</i>, <i>support</i>, <i>stabiliment</i> (very rare; not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haec sunt ventris stabilimenta, pane et assa
					bubula, Poclum grande,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 2, 3, 88</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">favorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 7, 6, § 16</span></i>
			. —* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sicilia et Sardinia stabilimenta bellorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 7, 6, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
